Solutions for (nearly) all the 2015 to 2025 Advent of Code puzzles.
Most years I first used Perl for a quick & dirty answer, then as I was learning Rust 
I have re-implemented most of them, trying for the most efficient code I could think of.
During the 2020-2024 years I worked for Cognite where we had an internal leaderboard, 
I had solved a few previous puzzles before this but after 2021 I went back and filled 
in all the missing years.

Besides Perl and RUst there are a couple of C(++) and Python solutions.

Usage: Every year/day has a separate sub-directory, the code expects to find input.txt
in each daily directory.

Perl: aoc(dd).pl input.txt
Rust: cargo run -r

Timing: All the solutions are self-timing, Perl does a single run while Rust typically 
picks the best from 25-1000 runs, with a few extremely fast (sub-10 us) codes measuring 
1000 iterations each time.